        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.092,
            0.882,
            0.111
          ],
          "content": "3. Explain how you chose the top­level test in the tree. The following table may be useful."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.115,
            0.583,
            0.229
          ],
          "content": "| x | y | ­(x/y)*lg(x/y) |  | x | y | ­(x/y)*lg(x/y) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 2 | 0.50 |  | 1 | 5 | 0.46 |\n| 1 | 3 | 0.53 |  | 2 | 5 | 0.53 |\n| 2 | 3 | 0.39 |  | 3 | 5 | 0.44 |\n| 1 | 4 | 0.50 |  | 4 | 5 | 0.26 |\n| 3 | 4 | 0.31 |  |  |  |  |",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.16,
                0.234,
                0.885,
                0.29
              ],
              "content": "Pick the decision boundary which falls halfway between each pair of adjacent points in each dimension, and which produces the minimum average entropy"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_table_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.362,
            0.327,
            0.684,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array}{r c l} A E & = & q _ {<  } H (p _ {<  }) + (1 - q _ {<  }) H (p _ {>}) \\\\ H (p) & = & - p \\lg (p) - (1 - p) \\lg (1 - p) \\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.412,
            0.885,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "where $q _ { < }$ is the fraction of points below the decision boundary, and $p _ { < } ,   p _ { \\geq }$ are the fraction of positive (+) points below and above the decision boundary, respectively."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.499,
            0.811,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array}{l l} f _ {2} > \\pm 0. 5: & A E = \\frac {1}{5} (0) + \\frac {4}{5} (1) = 0. 8 \\\\ f _ {1} > 1. 5: & A E = \\frac {3}{5} H \\left(\\frac {2}{3}\\right) + \\frac {2}{5} (0) = \\frac {3}{5} (0. 3 9 + 0. 5 3) = 0. 5 5 2 \\\\ f _ {1} > 0. 5: & A E = \\frac {2}{5} (1) + \\frac {3}{5} H \\left(\\frac {1}{3}\\right) = \\frac {2}{5} + \\frac {3}{5} (0. 3 9 + 0. 5 3) = 0. 9 5 2 \\\\ f _ {1} > - 0. 5: & A E = \\frac {1}{5} (0) + \\frac {4}{5} (1) = 0. 8 \\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.678,
            0.752,
            0.697
          ],
          "content": "4. What class does the decision tree predict for the new point: (1, ­1.01)"
